🚲 Bike Station Overview – Power BI Dashboard


📌 Project Overview
Public bike-sharing systems generate continuous real-time data across thousands of stations and multiple cities.
This project analyzes a bike station dataset using Power BI to understand station performance, utilization, availability, and operational efficiency.
The goal is to transform raw station-level data into actionable urban mobility insights that help operators improve service reliability, bike availability, and capacity planning.

🏷️ Domain
Urban Mobility Analytics | Transportation & Smart Cities

📂 Dataset Overview


Dataset Type: Real-time bike station snapshot


Coverage: Multiple cities (contracts)


Granularity: Station level


Total Stations: 2,700


Metrics Covered: Bikes, bike stands, station status, banking support



🛠️ Tools & Technologies


Power BI


DAX (Data Analysis Expressions)


Data Modeling (Fact & Dimension tables)



🔄 Project Workflow
1. Data Import & Modeling


Imported raw bike station data into Power BI


Defined relationships between fact and dimension tables


Ensured proper schema for accurate aggregations and filtering



2. DAX Measures & Calculated Metrics
Created key DAX measures to track system performance:


Total Stations


Available Bikes


Available Bike Stands


Bike Stand Capacity


Open Stations


Banking Stations


Overall Utilization %


Zero-Bike Stations


These measures enable real-time monitoring and drill-down analysis across cities.

📊 Executive Summary (Dashboard KPIs)
